       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. STEPDBCL.
      *> THE STEP D SECOND-GATE WIDENING (kb/Work PB164's LAST HALF;
      *> DESIGN-data-model 2.3 STEP D ITEM 4) - A BASED RECORD WITH A
      *> COMP LEAF IS ORDINARY, CELL-BACKED STORAGE. IT REPLACES THE
      *> NEGATIVE FIXTURE pb151-based-comp-leaf, WHICH PINNED THE OLD
      *> POSTURE (COBOLNET1695 AT BIND); THAT POSTURE REJECTED LEGAL
      *> COBOL. THE DERIVATION IS ONE-DIRECTIONAL:
      *>   13.18.5.3 SR1/SR2 - THE ONLY RESTRICTIONS ON THE SUBJECT OF
      *>   A BASED ENTRY ARE "SHALL NOT BE OF CLASS OBJECT" AND "SHALL
      *>   NOT BE A DYNAMIC-LENGTH ELEMENTARY ITEM OR A VARIABLE-LENGTH
      *>   GROUP". A GROUP WITH A COMP/COMP-3/COMP-1 LEAF IS NEITHER,
      *>   AND NO SYNTAX RULE ANYWHERE CONDITIONS BASED ON USAGE.
      *>   14.9.3.3 SR1 - ALLOCATE'S ONLY DEMAND ON data-name-1 IS THE
      *>   BASED CLAUSE; 14.9.3.4 GR3 - THE AMOUNT ALLOCATED IS "THE
      *>   NUMBER OF BYTES REQUIRED TO HOLD AN ITEM AS DESCRIBED BY
      *>   data-name-1" (2 + 2 + 4 = 8 HERE), A BYTE QUANTITY THE
      *>   USAGES ANSWER: 13.18.60.4 GR4 (BINARY, "A RADIX OF 2"),
      *>   GR11 (PACKED-DECIMAL, "A RADIX OF 10 ... THE MINIMUM
      *>   POSSIBLE CONFIGURATION"), AND THE PB164 WAVE-2 IEEE PIN.
      *> THE WINDOW IS READ OVER THE POINTER-DEREF BRIDGE - A SECOND
      *> BASED ENTRY ADDRESSING THE SAME CELL - WITH FUNCTION ORD
      *> (15.70.1: "THE ORDINAL POSITION OF argument-1 IN THE PROGRAM
      *> COLLATING SEQUENCE. THE LOWEST ORDINAL POSITION IS 1", SO ORD
      *> IS THE BYTE VALUE + 1), NEVER A SELF-INVERSE ROUND TRIP:
      *>   -2 IN S9(4) COMP  = FF FE (TWO'S COMPLEMENT, BIG-ENDIAN)
      *>   -123 IN S9(3) COMP-3 = 12 3D (BCD + THE D SIGN NIBBLE)
      *>   1.5 IN COMP-1     = 3F C0 00 00 (IEEE 754 binary32)
      *> THE BYTE->TYPED DIRECTION THEN PROVES THE CODEC IS AN
      *> INVOLUTION (THE R40 SIGN-LANE LESSON): BYTES WRITTEN THROUGH
      *> THE X VIEW WITH FUNCTION CHAR (15.15.1 - THE INVERSE OF ORD)
      *> DECODE AS 258 AND +223, AND FF FE READS BACK AS -2.
      *> FREE TAKES THE POINTER, NOT THE RECORD (14.9.15.3 SR1).
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 R BASED.
          05 R-N PIC S9(4) COMP.
          05 R-P PIC S9(3) COMP-3.
          05 R-F USAGE COMP-1.
       01 RB PIC X(8) BASED.
       01 WS-P USAGE POINTER.
       01 WS-V5 PIC 9(5).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           ALLOCATE R RETURNING WS-P
           SET ADDRESS OF RB TO WS-P
           MOVE -2 TO R-N
           MOVE -123 TO R-P
           MOVE 1.5 TO R-F
           DISPLAY FUNCTION ORD(RB(1:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RB(2:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(RB(3:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RB(4:1))
           DISPLAY FUNCTION ORD(RB(5:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RB(6:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(RB(7:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RB(8:1))
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(2) TO RB(1:1)
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(3) TO RB(2:1)
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(35) TO RB(3:1)
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(61) TO RB(4:1)
           MOVE R-N TO WS-V5
           DISPLAY WS-V5
           MOVE R-P TO WS-V5
           DISPLAY WS-V5
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(256) TO RB(1:1)
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(255) TO RB(2:1)
           IF R-N = -2
               DISPLAY "SIGN-OK"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "SIGN-BAD"
           END-IF
           FREE WS-P
           STOP RUN.
